cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the ACE paper it implements."
title: "ACE playbook: a measured lesson-to-hook compiler for CLI coding agents"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jasonmoorthy11-hub/ace-playbook"
authors:
  - family-names: Moorthy
    given-names: Jason
abstract: >-
  Stage 1 scaffold of an append-only lesson store, scrubber, injector and reflector
  for CLI coding agents, built around a pre-registered evaluation. It implements ideas
  from Agentic Context Engineering (Zhang et al., ICLR 2026). Not affiliated with or
  endorsed by the ACE authors or by Anthropic.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Agentic Context Engineering: Evolving Contexts for Self-Improving Language Models"
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhang
        given-names: Qizheng
      - name: "and co-authors (see the arXiv record)"
    year: 2026
    journal: "ICLR 2026"
    url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04618"
    notes: "arXiv:2510.04618. Reference implementation: https://github.com/ace-agent/ace"
